# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
target

# Debug-export and deadlock-dump artifacts written by the client into
# `<repo>/debug/` and `<crate>/debug/`. Ignore the contents (not the
# directory itself) so audit progress — which lives in the same folder
# — can be re-included by the rule below. Git cannot un-ignore a file
# inside an excluded directory, hence the `debug/*` form over plain
# `debug`.
debug/*
**/debug/*

# Audit progress is tracked across sessions. The audit feature
# (crabomination_client::audit) writes a JSON list of verified card names
# to debug/audited_cards.json — keep it under version control so the
# team's verification state survives across machines.
!**/audited_cards.json

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Card images are auto-downloaded from Scryfall on first run by
# `crabomination_client::scryfall::ensure_card_images`; tracking them just
# bloats the repo and goes stale when the catalog grows. Fonts stay tracked
# (they're not auto-fetched and the UI needs them at startup).
crabomination_client/assets/cards/

# Per-user Claude Code harness settings (allow-lists, hooks, etc.).
# Each contributor maintains their own.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python bytecode cache from running scripts/*.py (audit_strixhaven2.py,
# verify_cards.py, etc.). Auto-generated by the interpreter; never tracked.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
*.log

# Session scratch files (oracle dumps, set diffs) — never tracked.
scratch_*

# Scratch gap-analysis dumps from scripts/fin_gaps.py.
scripts/.*_missing.json
web/dist/

# Ladder scratch: gate output, logs, and calibration dumps are large,
# regenerable, and per-machine. The run scripts are NOT scratch — every
# ML_NOTES round entry cites one as its pre-registration, and a
# pre-registration nobody can read afterwards is not one. Track those.
.ladder/*
!.ladder/run_*.sh

# Training checkpoints. Each net directory is tens of megabytes of
# weights plus a stats stream; they are run artifacts, reproducible from
# the run script and the seed. `nets/champion.safetensors` is tracked
# deliberately (the client and the ladder default to it) and is not
# matched by this.
/nets_*/

# Editor / rescue leftovers. A stray 700 KB `tests/sos_old.rs.bak` sat in
# the tree for weeks before it was noticed; keep the class out.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# Side-by-side target dir for allocator A/B builds (see PERF.md).
/target-mi/
# Side-by-side target dir for A/B perf builds: a second CARGO_TARGET_DIR lets
# a `profiling-fast` build and a callgrind run overlap (see PERF.md).
/target-probe/

# callgrind / profiling output
cg*.out
callgrind.out.*
# callgrind_annotate dumps — `ann.txt`, `ann.base.txt`, `tree.d.txt`, …
# The list grew because `git add -A` committed three of them twice now
# (`797040ba`, `3d15878b`); one name per `--tree=` / `--inclusive=` mode.
ann*.txt
tree*.txt
self*.txt
incl*.txt
tc*.txt
# Fourth time (`304d16bf`): the pattern list will keep losing this race, so
# write annotate dumps to the session scratchpad, not the repo root.

calling*.txt

# callgrind dumps and their symbolized copies (see PERF.md "How to measure")
cg.*.out
cg.*.sym
cg.out
